BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tomas Gonda
DTSTART:20261203T170000Z
DTEND:20261203T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20261111T161545Z
UID:ToposInstituteColloquium/236
DESCRIPTION:Title: <a href="https://researchseminars.org/talk/ToposInstitu
 teColloquium/236/">Ergodic Theory\, categorically</a>\nby Tomas Gonda as p
 art of Topos Institute Colloquium\n\nInteractive livestream: https://topos
 -institute.zoom.us/j/00000000000?pwd=REDACTEDREDACTEDREDACTEDREDACTED\nPas
 sword hint: 00000\n\nAbstract\nIn recent years\, categorical treatments of
  famous theorems about properties of invariant measures have emerged. Amon
 g them are the de Finetti Theorem\, the strong law of large numbers and er
 godic decompositions. Here\, we synthesize these developments by introduci
 ng the concept of a mixing morphism for an abstract dynamical system in a 
 Markov category. It axiomatizes the idea of finding an average of the dyna
 mics that is itself invariant\, which is closely tied to the Pointwise Erg
 odic Theorem. In this talk\, we will explore the abstract consequences of 
 having a mixing morphism as well as several concrete instantiations in fam
 iliar Markov categories - for general probabilistic systems\, linear syste
 ms with Gaussian noise\, and possibilistic uncertainty.\n
LOCATION:https://researchseminars.org/talk/ToposInstituteColloquium/236/
URL:https://topos-institute.zoom.us/j/00000000000?pwd=REDACTEDREDACTEDREDA
 CTEDREDACTED
END:VEVENT
